@bank all
// SW3 (2026-10-26, Pillar 5 Step 5, S5-5 words; spec section 10): M20 The sensor array (24x), Friday Day 19, 10:00-12:00,
// Deck 2's array room (A) with Hana Mori (she/her) and Calder. The training is meeting train.m20.mori; "Pick the star"
// is a device card (m20.pick.*); the rig is WORK_TOOLS.arrayrig. Mori's step words are her own lines, flags
// train.m20.follow.*. Said by nobody unless noted. 24t's logged stars are named "Wren {n}"; the five reference stars
// below are the array's own (no capital-letter names but Tavessa, the cluster ahead: every star has a Veyli name too).

== works.mech.m20
- The sensor array
== works.ask.m20
- The sensor array | Hana Mori in Survey has asked for you. Calibrating the array against a star. I'll come too. {time}, {place}.
== next.m20
- The sensor array comes next: Deck 2's array room, with Hana Mori from Survey.
== next.wait.m20
- The sensor array: meet Hana Mori in the array room, Deck 2.
== m20.ptr
- The sensor array with Hana Mori, {time}
== m20.notice
- The sensor array with Hana Mori at {time}: the array room, Deck 2. Go at quarter to.

// the rig given (toast), its name and its line (the Tools page)
== m20.rig.give
- Hana Mori gave you the calibration rig. Survey's spare, now yours.
== works.tool.arrayrig
- Calibration rig
== works.tool.arrayrig.about
- A dial and a reading. Point the array at a known star and turn till they agree.

// "Pick the star": the card, the five stars (a short name for the button, and Mori's line when you pick it)
== m20.pick.title
- Pick the star
== m20.pick.text
- Hana has three reference stars in view. Pick one to calibrate against.
== m20.star.1
- Tavessa's brightest
== m20.star.1.line
- The brightest in Tavessa. It's steady. Steady is what we want.
== m20.star.2
- The white one, low
== m20.star.2.line
- Low and white. Very quiet star. It never surprises anyone.
== m20.star.3
- The old red giant
== m20.star.3.line
- Big and red and slow. It breathes, a little. Watch the reading.
== m20.star.4
- The close pair
== m20.star.4.line
- Two stars, very close. Pick the left one. Everyone picks the right.
== m20.star.5
- The one behind us
== m20.star.5.line
- We passed it six weeks ago. It's still the best-measured star we have.
// the star you picked is one you logged (24t), if the builder can tell ({star}: its log name)
== m20.star.yours
- That's in your own star log: {star}. Hana noticed before you did.

// the calibration (tuning's dial, 24e's turn control)
== m20.cal.title
- Calibrate · {machine}
== m20.cal.text
- Turn the dial till the array's reading and the star agree.
== m20.cal.far
- Far off. Keep turning.
== m20.cal.close
- Close. Small turns now.
== m20.cal.on
- On the star. The array agrees.
// replace a failing module (the racks: 2-racks-1, -2)
== m20.module.title
- Array rack · {machine}
== m20.module.look
- One module's light is amber. The rest are green.
== m20.module.swap
- Swap the amber module
== m20.module.done
- All green. The array sees cleanly again.
// stages and the friendship moment
== m20.trained.stage2
- The sensor array: you can run a full sweep now.
== m20.trained.stage3
- The sensor array: your sweeps feed Survey's charts now.
== m20.sweep.done
- Full sweep done. Survey has your readings.
